  "turns": [
    {
      "_id": "0",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Let's look at this one: a recipe uses flour and sugar in a 3 to 5 ratio, and we're told 12 cups of flour are used.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s01-t001",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:00:00.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:00:22.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "1",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 2,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So we know the ratio is 3 to 5, and the flour amount is 12 cups.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s01-t002",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:00:25.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:00:54.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "2",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 3,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Right, and the question wants us to find how much sugar goes with that 12 cups of flour.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s01-t003",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:00:54.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:01:28.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "3",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 4,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Got it — find the sugar amount that matches 12 cups of flour.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s01-t004",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:01:34.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:02:34.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "4",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 5,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Before we dive in, did you end up making anything with your family this weekend?",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s01-t005",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:02:34.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:03:16.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "5",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 6,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Actually let's get into it — the ratio means for every 3 cups of flour there are 5 cups of sugar.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s01-t006",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:03:21.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:04:17.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "6",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 7,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Exactly, the two amounts scale together, so 12 cups of flour is just a multiple of that 3.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s01-t007",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:04:21.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:05:22.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "7",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 8,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So whatever flour we use, it has to stay in that same 3 to 5 proportion with the sugar.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s01-t008",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:05:28.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:05:58.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "8",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 9,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That means we can think of the recipe in equal 'parts' — 3 parts flour and 5 parts sugar.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s01-t009",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:05:58.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:07:00.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "9",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 10,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So one part of flour and one part of sugar are always the same size unit.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s01-t010",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:07:04.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:07:46.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "10",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 11,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Right, and since 12 cups equals those 3 parts of flour, we can figure out what a single part weighs.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s01-t011",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:07:50.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:09:00.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "11",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 12,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Once we know one part in cups, we can just use that to get the sugar side too.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s01-t012",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:09:07.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:09:41.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "12",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 13,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That's the key relationship — parts stay proportional however much you scale the recipe.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s01-t013",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:09:49.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:10:07.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "13",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 14,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So I think our first move should be figuring out how many cups one part is worth.",
      "turn_id": "demo-b-s01-t014",
      "start_time": "2026-01-13T16:10:15.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-01-13T16:11:13.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "14",
      "session_id": "demo-b-s01",
      "sequence_id": 15,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Good instinct — go ahead and find that value from the flour side first.",
